JCI class/attribute reference dictionaries in backend/bms_tool/data are adapted
from thecontrolscompany/oct (Apache-2.0), commit c1d76ba7d6a8f17ca089c4671fa3333e4eba43e2.
Upstream: https://github.com/thecontrolscompany/oct
The original Apache license is retained in third_party/OCT-LICENSE.txt.
Mappings are interoperability references, not a vendor SDK or compiler.
No JCI binaries, controller applications, credentials, or manuals are redistributed.

The optional native compiler/simulator integrates linsong/sedona, commit
406b11f3816fb00db6482640f9cf3397b874b515, copyright 2006-2013 Tridium, Inc.
Upstream: https://github.com/linsong/sedona
Its Academic Free License 3.0 and trademark notice are retained in
third_party/Sedona-LICENSE.md. The SDK source is downloaded separately;
scripts/setup_sedona.py reproduces modifications to the compiler's reference
layout/null optimization and the SVM's null-pointer/UDP ABI handling. The native
simulation build binds sockets to loopback. This experimental port is not a
Sedona-certified platform. Generated application bundles contain an upstream
license copy and source/build provenance for their included SCode runtime.

The optional Temco Control Basic compiler/interpreter host builds separate
copies of manufacturer source from temcocontrols/T3000_Building_Automation_System,
revision ae9b9d082de93b35ff2ca59eb1d0c06ae04cec9b. Upstream:
https://github.com/temcocontrols/T3000_Building_Automation_System
The upstream MIT license is retained in third_party/Temco-T3000-LICENSE.txt.
scripts/setup_temco.py records the host adaptations. Upstream source and built
executables stay outside this repository. This host has no field transport.

The Niagara BOG adapter uses the public MIT pybog implementation as an encoding
reference, revision 0248d941bf230aad2f19f9805be67c0e64bd51ef, copyright 2025
Ben Bartling. Upstream: https://github.com/bbartling/pybog
The original license is retained in third_party/pybog-LICENSE.txt. No Niagara
SDK, runtime, keys or protected station data is bundled. Native station acceptance
and event/status/priority equivalence remain unverified.

The separately written Python MS/TP driver was reviewed against BACnet-stack
and tested with externally compiled frame encoders. No BACnet-stack C code or
binaries are bundled or loaded at runtime. File-level source, license and test
provenance is recorded in docs/mstp-provenance.md.

The optional IEC verifier invokes the external MatIEC compiler, revision
3a41303bcb4e50403417bc39c63f88981d7d961e, from https://github.com/beremiz/matiec.
The compiler is GPL-3.0-or-later; individual runtime headers retain their LGPL
notices. scripts/setup_iec.py obtains/builds this dependency separately without
changing the pinned source. No compiler, runtime headers or generated native
executable is redistributed in this repository. See docs/iec-native.md.

The original Python Temco program-transfer adapter references manufacturer wire
layouts in T3000 and ESP32 controller source, revision
845973a37b91ac5ddac9c465787f2ab3a5037708 at
https://github.com/temcocontrols/T3-programmable-controller-on-ESP32.
Independent fixtures use external unchanged BACnet C encoders; their source
and binaries are not bundled or loaded by the application. See
docs/temco-transfer.md for file-level provenance and verification limits.
